  ("How old is too old for a furnace in a Scarborough bungalow?", "Most gas furnaces last about 15 to 20 years, so a unit from the 1990s or earlier is due for a replacement plan. If the heat exchanger shows cracks or a repair costs a big share of a new furnace, replacing is usually the smarter move."),
  ("Will my bungalow's original ducts work with a heat pump?", "Yes, in most post-war bungalows and side-splits. We check static pressure first, because some older duct systems need a few runs upsized before they can carry a heat pump's airflow."),
